    "summary": "Hydria Device Access",
    "description": "Network access work for the **Hydria / Composite Advanced Technology** deployment (via TAS Industries).\n\n**Tunnel:** Hydria-Composite — private network `10.80.1.0/24` (fully private, no internet breakout).\n**Device:** Teltonika RUT956 on OptConnect SIM at `10.80.1.4/32`; reachable via OpenVPN, no internet.\n\n**Goal:** enable the modem(s) to reach the customer's MQTT broker without granting public internet access — by bringing the customer's AWS MQTT server into the private tunnel as a dedicated OpenVPN client.\n\n**Requested by customer (Venkatesh, TAS — 2026-07-16), to be delivered as child tasks:**\n\n* Dedicated OpenVPN client profile + credentials for the AWS server (separate identity from their admin VPN, which must stay online continuously)\n* Fixed OpenVPN tunnel IP for that client (CCD static IP)\n* Route allowing `10.80.1.0/24` ↔ AWS server tunnel IP\n* Permit TCP 1883 (MQTT) from `10.80.1.0/24` → server tunnel IP\n* Confirm client-to-client (SIM ↔ VPN-client) communication enabled\n* Provide OpenVPN server protocol + port the AWS security group must allow outbound\n\nRef: email thread \"Re: No internet connection\" (m2msupport / net-eng, Jul 2026). Contacts: m.venkatesh@tasind.com, suyash.bhongle@tasind.com, dcampos@gohydria.com.",
